# mypiggles.com — the Piggles console. Copy to `.env` for local development.
#
# ── WHY THIS FILE IS NOT OPTIONAL ───────────────────────────────────────────
#
# The console renders its panes in the BROWSER, and api-rest authenticates a
# staff caller by exactly one credential: a short-lived HS256 JWT minted at
# `/api/token`. That route needs two variables and refuses to mint anything
# without them:
#
#     if (!secret || !apiUrl) return 500 'misconfigured'
#
# With no `.env` the route 500s, `fetchToken` throws "Could not start a secure
# session (500)", and EVERY pane in the workspace fails at once — a console that
# renders perfectly, navigates perfectly, and cannot load a single row. Nothing
# in typecheck, lint or a build says a word about it.
#
# This is the same shape of failure as the account app's missing BETTER_AUTH_URL
# (piggles/STATUS.md, "THE LOCKOUT"): a file that does not exist, defaults that
# are wrong, and a symptom that points somewhere else entirely.

# ── api-rest ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL is the origin the BROWSER calls directly with the bearer
# token, so it must be reachable from the browser — never an in-cluster service
# address. It is also inlined at BUILD time, so changing it needs a rebuild
# rather than a restart.
SPARX_API_REST_URL="http://localhost:3100"
NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL="http://localhost:3100"

# Must match api-rest's own secret — this app mints the internal JWTs api-rest
# verifies. Both brands' consoles talk to the SAME api-rest, so this value is
# the platform's, not Piggles'.
SPARX_INTERNAL_JWT_SECRET="dev-only-internal-jwt-secret-change-me-32chars"

# ── Better Auth ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# The console mounts NO Better Auth handler and has no sign-in UI — getpiggles
# is the auth authority and this app receives a session through the handoff
# (piggles/CLAUDE.md, "Cross-domain auth"). It still READS the session
# server-side and calls the organization endpoints for the business switcher, so
# the auth instance has to know which origin it is running on.
#
# Must be the SAME secret as the account app: both read and write the same
# Better Auth session rows, and a differing secret makes every session
# unverifiable.
BETTER_AUTH_URL="http://localhost:3022"
BETTER_AUTH_SECRET="ZTtjC/n97adyGwtmyjGqgiGcJ2EQVziS+fHGkxX7V2U="

# MUST MATCH THE ACCOUNT APP'S. This console does not issue the session cookie —
# it READS the one getpiggles.com set, and the cookie's name is how it finds it.
# A mismatch is not an error anywhere: `getSession()` simply returns null, the
# console decides nobody is signed in, and it bounces every arriving customer
# straight back to the account app in a loop.
BETTER_AUTH_COOKIE_PREFIX="piggles-account"

# Where an unauthenticated visitor is bounced to, and where "Manage account",
# billing and sign-out lead. Production is https://getpiggles.com.
PIGGLES_ACCOUNT_ORIGIN="http://localhost:3021"

# ── Database ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
DATABASE_URL="postgresql://sparx_app:devpassword@localhost:5544/sparx?schema=public"
AUTH_DATABASE_URL="postgresql://sparx_owner:devpassword@localhost:5544/sparx?schema=public"

# Local-dev only: keeps the site editor's Preview on this machine instead of
# opening the tenant's canonical domain, which is real DNS pointing at
# production. Leave UNSET in every deployed environment.
NEXT_PUBLIC_STOREFRONT_ORIGIN="http://localhost:3004"
